cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "EXOTIC-CCR A001: Poisson/Weyl lifts and bounded Lean-backed Theorems E-F"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fredriksen
    given-names: Daniel Eric
    affiliation: "Quantyra Inc"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21474351
version: "0.3.8-theorem-f"
url: "https://github.com/Quantyra/jacobian-weyl-quantum-phase-space"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Quantyra/jacobian-weyl-quantum-phase-space"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - jacobian-conjecture
  - deficiency-indices
  - essential-self-adjointness
  - exotic-ccr
abstract: >-
  Poisson/Weyl lifts of the Alpoge-Fable Keller seed (restated). H=-i X_1 not ESS
  with deficiency indices (infinity, infinity) via whole-orbit deficiency vectors.
  The companion Lean artifact proves the bounded canonical-core Theorem E via
  ExoticCCR.theoremE (tag v0.1.8-theorem-e, SHA a6bb091) and, proposed and under
  review, the bounded Theorem F via ExoticCCR.theoremF at SHA
  f1fe83785add60ccc5f012b51e7576aab5627a74: both
  adjoint eigenspaces ker(H-dagger -+ i) of the canonical minimal core are
  infinite-dimensional, obtained by a measure-preserving sign-involution
  transport of the forward minus-i families. A separate `hilbertDeficiencyIndex`
  result at that SHA proves `hilbertDeficiencyIndex_X1_eq_aleph0` for the
  closed adjoint eigenspaces. `standardDeficiencyIndex` is `Module.rank`, the
  algebraic (Hamel) rank, for which the standard cardinal-valued lower bounds
  Cardinal.aleph0 ≤ n_+ and Cardinal.aleph0 ≤ n_- are recorded but exact
  equality is not claimed. Von Neumann extension multiplicity/classification
  and the paper's backward-wall construction remain not Lean-covered. Prior
  withdrawn: v0.2.2 pair (0,infinity); v0.3.0
  s-indicator proof. No gates/channels. This is a proposed untagged review
  artifact; no new version DOI is asserted.
